<title>GERMANY: Henkel starts 97 well, no Loctite woes.</title>
<headline>Henkel starts 97 well, no Loctite woes.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemical group Henkel KGaA said on Monday its 1997 business year had started well.</p>
<p>&quot;The first quarter results are good,&quot; the group said in the text of the speech to be delivered at its shareholders meeting.</p>
<p>No negative market or customer reactions had been experienced relating to its takeover of U.S.-based glue-maker Loctite, it added.</p>
<p>The restructuring of its chemical products division would also be a goal in this and the coming year, the group said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
